MARKDOWN.append((
    '## Estimated Runtime By Runnable Cell\n'
    '\n'
    '\n'
    "The size guidance below uses the same order-of-magnitude heuristic as the command-line preflight report: median model-family wall-clock times from the manuscript's Table 6, scaled roughly linearly with molecule count from a 1,605-molecule reference dataset. It is meant to prevent surprises, not to promise an exact finish time.\n"
    '\n'
    '| Valid molecules after cleaning | Practical interpretation | Core path (`0`-`4D`) | Expensive options to treat carefully |\n'
    '| ---: | --- | ---: | --- |\n'
    '| `<500` | Tiny tutorial or pilot set | usually 5-20 min after setup | GA tuning and deep models are feasible experiments, but still optional. |\n'
    '| `500-2,000` | Typical small QSAR project | usually 10-45 min after setup | Uni-Mol/Chemprop can become the dominant runtime; use GPU and modest epochs. |\n'
    '| `2,000-10,000` | Medium dataset | usually 30 min-2 h after setup | ElasticNetCV, GA tuning, Chemprop, Uni-Mol, and applicability-domain fitting can take hours. |\n'
    '| `10,000-50,000` | Large interactive notebook job | several hours is plausible | Prefer random-forest feature-selection fallback, fewer model families, and command-line/batch mode for long runs. |\n'
    '| `>50,000` | Better suited to batch/HPC | not recommended for a beginner notebook run | Use `qsarena-benchmark --dry-run` first and plan compute before training. |\n'
    '\n'
    'Approximate per-model-family medians at the 1,605-row reference size were: conventional ML about 7 s per model, ChemML MLP about 40 s, MapLight + GNN about 137 s, Chemprop about 269 s per variant, and Uni-Mol about 374 s. A block that trains several models multiplies those per-model costs, and CPU-only deep learning may be several times slower.\n'
    '\n'
    '| Cell | Typical time | Notes |\n'
    '| --- | ---: | --- |\n'
    '| `0` Setup | 2-12 min | First run may install packages and restart; cached environments are faster. |\n'
    '| `1A` Load data | 5 sec-3 min | Example datasets that download from external sources can take longer. |\n'
    '| `1B` Choose columns | <5 sec | Mostly validation and preview. |\n'
    '| `1C` Missingness, curation, target transform | 10 sec-3 min | Larger datasets and difficult SMILES curation can take longer. |\n'
    '| `2A` Molecule preview | 5-30 sec | RDKit drawing time depends on preview count. |\n'
    '| `2B` Generate molecular features | 30 sec-10 min | Heavier feature families and uncached MapLight-style features increase runtime/RAM. |\n'
    '| `3A` Similarity map | 30 sec-8 min | t-SNE/embedding cost grows with molecule count and selected features. |\n'
    '| `4A` Split train/test | 5 sec-2 min | Scaffold splitting can be slower than random or target-quartile splitting. |\n'
    '| `4A.5` Configure feature selection | <10 sec | Stores selector settings. |\n'
    '| `4B` Run feature selection | 30 sec-20 min | ElasticNetCV can be slow for high feature counts; RF fallback is safer for quick interactive runs. |\n'
    '| `4C` Train conventional models | 2-30 min | Depends on selected models, CV, rows, and feature count. |\n'
    '| `4D` Plot conventional predictions | 5-30 sec | Usually quick. |\n'
    '| `4E` GA tuning | 10 min-2+ hr | Optional; model count, generations, population size, and CV dominate runtime. |\n'
    '| `4F` Plot tuned predictions | 5-30 sec | Usually quick. |\n'
    '| `4G` GA convergence plots | 5-30 sec | Usually quick. |\n'
    '| `5A` GPU check | <5 sec | Reports runtime hardware. |\n'
    '| `5A.5` TabPFN auth check | 10 sec-2 min | Optional; depends on API/client availability. |\n'
    '| `5B` Deep-learning models | 5-60+ min | GPU recommended; MapLight + GNN and TabPFN can be compatibility-sensitive. |\n'
    '| `5C` Compare deep/conventional | 5-30 sec | Uses completed model results. |\n'
    '| `6A` Install Uni-Mol packages | 1-10 min | May require runtime restart. |\n'
    '| `6B` Prepare Uni-Mol files | 5 sec-2 min | Mostly file writing and split preparation. |\n'
    '| `6C` Uni-Mol V1 | 10 min-2+ hr | Optional; GPU only (skipped without a GPU). |\n'
    '| `6D` Uni-Mol V2 | 20 min-3+ hr | GPU strongly recommended; larger model sizes can exceed notebook memory. |\n'
    '| `6E` Install Chemprop v2 | 1-10 min | May require runtime restart. |\n'
    '| `6F` Chemprop v2 variants | 10 min-2+ hr | Optional; GPU only (skipped without a GPU). |\n'
    '| `6G` Plot Uni-Mol predictions | 5-30 sec | Usually quick. |\n'
    '| `6H` Compare model families | 5-60 sec | Usually quick. |\n'
    '| `7A` Build ensemble | 30 sec-10 min | Depends on available member models and ensemble method. |\n'
    '| `7B` Plot ensemble | 5-30 sec | Usually quick. |\n'
    '| `8A` Configure explanations | <10 sec | Stores explanation settings. |\n'
    '| `8B` Explain conventional model | 30 sec-15 min | SHAP/permutation settings and feature count dominate runtime. |\n'
    '| `8C` Explain ChemML deep model | 30 sec-20 min | DeepSHAP/LIME/LRP can be slow on CPU. |\n'
    '| `9A` Predict new molecules | 10 sec-10 min | Optional; Uni-Mol/Chemprop predictions can be slower than conventional models. |\n'
    '| `9B` Prediction UMAP | 30 sec-8 min | Optional; grows with train/test plus new molecules. |\n'
    '| `9D` Applicability domain | 5-60+ min | Optional; MADML fitting and repeated validation can be expensive. |\n'
    '| `9F` Export HTML report | 5-30 sec | Collects completed notebook outputs into one shareable HTML file. |\n'
))

