MARKDOWN.append((
    '### 2B. Generate Molecular Features\n'
    '\n'
    'Select one or more molecular feature families below. Checking every box is the equivalent of an "all descriptors" representation.\n'
    '\n'
    '**Safe beginner defaults:** for a first run, use **Morgan fingerprints**, **MACCS keys**, and **RDKit descriptors**. Leave MapLight classic and the extra fingerprint families off if memory becomes tight or feature generation is slow. You can always rerun this block with more feature families after the core workflow works.\n'
    '\n'
    '**Avalon note:** there is no separate Avalon checkbox because Avalon-count fingerprints are already included inside **MapLight classic** (`maplight` family), alongside Morgan-count, ErG, and MapLight descriptor blocks.\n'
    '\n'
    'This block now uses a persistent molecular feature store by default. The store is an append-only Parquet layout that keeps previously generated feature rows keyed by:\n'
    '\n'
    '- canonical SMILES\n'
    '- selected feature families\n'
    '- fingerprint settings relevant to those families\n'
    '\n'
    'Internally, each representation gets its own folder with:\n'
    '\n'
    '- a schema file describing the feature columns\n'
    '- append-only Parquet shard files for newly generated rows\n'
    '\n'
    'When you rerun feature generation, the notebook first checks that store. Existing rows are loaded immediately, and only missing rows are newly generated and appended to the store.\n'
))

MARKDOWN.append((
    '### Before You Run: 2B. Build Molecular Features\n'
    '\n'
    '**What this does.** Converts each molecule into numeric fingerprints and descriptors that machine-learning models can use.\n'
    '\n'
    '**Main choices.** For a first run, Morgan, MACCS, and RDKit descriptors are a good balance. More fingerprint families may improve coverage but increase RAM, feature-selection time, and model training time. MapLight classic is useful for benchmark parity but can be heavier.\n'
    '\n'
    '**Time cost.** About 30 seconds to 10 minutes for typical tutorial datasets. Large datasets and many feature families can take much longer, especially without cache reuse.\n'
    '\n'
    '**What to expect.** Feature matrix dimensions, feature-family summaries, and stored feature metadata for later cells.\n'
    '\n'
    '#### Why these defaults?\n'
    '\n'
    '| Option | Default | Benchmark | Status | Why |\n'
    '| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n'
    '| `use_morgan_features` | on | on (all families built) | **Lighter** | The benchmark built all 11 families and let selection choose. Morgan (ECFP4) was the least enriched family among selected features (0.31x uniform) but is cheap and selected on 38/44 datasets. |\n'
    '| `use_ecfp6_features` | off | on | **Lighter** | Off to keep the matrix small. Enrichment among selected features 0.53x. |\n'
    '| `use_fcfp6_features` | off | on | **Lighter** | Off to keep the matrix small. Enrichment 0.73x. |\n'
    '| `use_layered_features` | off | on | **Lighter** | Off to keep the matrix small. Enrichment 0.48x. |\n'
    '| `use_atom_pair_features` | off | on | **Lighter** | Off to keep the matrix small. Enrichment 0.66x. |\n'
    '| `use_topological_torsion_features` | off | on | **Lighter** | Off to keep the matrix small. Enrichment 0.56x. |\n'
    '| `use_rdk_path_features` | off | on | **Lighter** | Off to keep the matrix small. Enrichment 0.62x. |\n'
    '| `use_maccs_keys` | on | on | **Evidence** | Small (167 bits) and slightly over-selected (1.18x). |\n'
    '| `use_rdkit_descriptors` | on | on | **Evidence** | The most over-selected family in the benchmark (5.16x uniform; picked on 40/44 datasets). |\n'
    '| `use_maplight_classic` | on | on | **Evidence** | On, as in the benchmark. Its Avalon and ErG parts were among the most over-selected families (2.5x, 2.9x uniform), it supplied 46% of selected features from 23% of those available, adding it improved the best model on 10/44 datasets, and it enables MapLight CatBoost, the single model with the lowest median regression gap (4.5%). It costs little: about 4.5 s for 642 molecules, the same as the RDKit descriptors. |\n'
    '| `morgan_radius` | `2` | 2 | **Benchmark** | Radius 2 (ECFP4), as in the benchmark. |\n'
    '| `fingerprint_bits` | `1024` | 1024 | **Benchmark** | 1024 bits, as in the benchmark. |\n'
    '| `enable_persistent_feature_store` | on | on | **No effect** | Caching only: rebuilt features are identical. |\n'
    '| `reuse_persistent_feature_store` | on | on | **No effect** | Caching only. |\n'
    '| `persistent_feature_store_path` | `AUTO` |  | **No effect** | Cache location. |\n'
))

