MARKDOWN.append((
    '## 4. Conventional QSAR Models\n'
    '\n'
    'This section follows the same broad modeling logic used throughout the repository:\n'
    '\n'
    '- build a numerical representation from SMILES\n'
    '- split data into training and test sets\n'
    '- optionally run the train-only feature selector configured in `4A.5`\n'
    '- use scaling where the model benefits from it\n'
    '- compare several algorithms with the **same split**\n'
    '- judge the final models by both cross-validation and held-out test performance\n'
    '\n'
    'The selector follows the stronger pattern from the QSAR references in `refs/`: split first, fit feature selection on the training data only, then evaluate the selected representation on held-out test data.\n'
))

MARKDOWN.append((
    '### Before You Run: 4A. Split The Dataset\n'
    '\n'
    '**What this does.** Separates molecules into training rows used to fit models and test rows held back for final checking.\n'
    '\n'
    '**Main choices.** Scaffold split is chemically stricter and often harder; random split is faster and easier but can overestimate real-world performance; target-quartile split balances a continuous target. Keep the same split when comparing model families.\n'
    '\n'
    '**Time cost.** Usually seconds; scaffold splitting can take minutes on larger datasets.\n'
    '\n'
    '**What to expect.** Train/test counts and target-distribution diagnostics.\n'
    '\n'
    '#### Why these defaults?\n'
    '\n'
    '| Option | Default | Benchmark | Status | Why |\n'
    '| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n'
    "| `data_split_strategy` | `target_quartiles` | official split where one exists | **Untested** | The benchmark used each suite's official split on 27/44 datasets, scaffold on 12, target quartiles on 4 and random on 1, so it never compared strategies. Target quartiles keep the full target range in the test set. Use `predefined` for an official split, or `scaffold` for a harder, more realistic test on new chemotypes. |\n"
    '| `test_fraction` | `0.2` | 0.2 | **Benchmark** | 20% held out, as in the benchmark wherever it made its own split. |\n'
    '| `model_random_seed` | `42` | 13 | **No effect** | Seed. The benchmark used 13; any fixed value gives a reproducible split. |\n'
))

