    "| `unimol_max_atoms` | `96` | 64 | **Untested** | Larger than the benchmark's 64, so fewer large molecules are truncated, at the cost of GPU memory. Use 64 if memory is tight. |\n"
    '| `unimol_use_amp` | on | on | **Benchmark** | Mixed precision, as in the benchmark. |\n'
    '| `unimol_num_workers` | `0` | 8 | **No effect** | Data-loading workers only. 0 avoids worker crashes in Colab and on Windows. |\n'
