MARKDOWN.append((
    '### Safe Beginner Defaults For Chemprop\n'
    '\n'
    'Start with one graph variant, keep `chemprop_epochs` modest, and leave RDKit2D extras off unless you need them. Chemprop can be package-sensitive, so after `6E` installs or upgrades packages, a runtime/kernel restart is often the cleanest path.\n'
))

MARKDOWN.append((
    '### Before You Run: 6F. Chemprop Variants\n'
    '\n'
    '**What this does.** Trains one or more Chemprop graph neural-network variants.\n'
    '\n'
    '**Main choices.** Start with one variant and modest epochs. Each added variant and ensemble member adds training time. Descriptor-augmented variants need the selected descriptor matrix from earlier cells.\n'
    '\n'
    '**Time cost.** Often 10 minutes to 2+ hours on a GPU. Skipped without a GPU: on CPU each variant takes roughly 8 times longer.\n'
    '\n'
    '**What to expect.** Chemprop metrics for completed variants and actionable errors for variants that fail.\n'
    '\n'
    '#### Why these defaults?\n'
    '\n'
    '| Option | Default | Benchmark | Status | Why |\n'
    '| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n'
    '| `enable_chemprop_model_cache` | on |  | **No effect** | Caching only. |\n'
    '| `reuse_chemprop_cached_models` | on |  | **No effect** | Caching only. |\n'
    '| `chemprop_run_label` | `AUTO` |  | **No effect** | Cache name. |\n'
    "| `run_chemprop_dmpnn` | on | on | **Evidence** | The best Chemprop variant for regression (4 wins, median gap 9.0%); mid-table for classification (5.5%). On by default because this notebook's examples are regression tasks. |\n"
    '| `run_chemprop_cmpnn` | off | on | **Lighter** | No wins in either task (10.8% regression, 7.0% classification). |\n'
    '| `run_chemprop_attentivefp` | on | on | **Evidence** | The best Chemprop variant for classification (4 wins, median gap 2.9%); 11.6% for regression. |\n'
    '| `run_chemprop_rdkit2d_extra` | off | on | **Lighter** | Second-best Chemprop variant for classification (3.6%). |\n'
    '| `run_chemprop_selected_features` | off | on | **Evidence** | Off: the weakest Chemprop variant in both tasks (median gap 21.2% regression vs 9.0% for plain D-MPNN; 5.0% classification), with no wins on any of 44 datasets. Adding the selected descriptors to the graph model made it worse, not better, so it is not worth the extra ~4.5 min per run. Turn it on only to study descriptor-augmented graphs. |\n'
    '| `chemprop_epochs` | `15` | 40 | **Lighter** | The RTX run used 15, like this default. That comparison does not isolate Chemprop, so use 40 when Chemprop is the model you care about. |\n'
    '| `chemprop_batch_size` | `32` | 32 | **Benchmark** | As in the benchmark. |\n'
    '| `chemprop_num_workers` | `0` | 8 | **No effect** | Data-loading workers only. Must stay 0 on Windows, where each worker reloads CUDA and can exhaust memory. |\n'
    '| `chemprop_ensemble_size` | `1` | 3 | **Lighter** | The benchmark averaged 3 models per variant; 1 is three times faster. |\n'
    '| `chemprop_random_seed` | `42` | 42 | **Benchmark** | As in the benchmark. |\n'
))

