MARKDOWN.append((
    '## 8. Model Explanation\n'
    '\n'
    'Model explanation answers a different question than model accuracy.\n'
    '\n'
    '- **Accuracy** asks whether predictions are reliable.\n'
    '- **Explanation** asks which molecular patterns the model appears to rely on.\n'
    '\n'
    'In this tutorial:\n'
    '\n'
    '- the best conventional model is explained with **feature importance**\n'
    "- the ChemML PyTorch neural network is explained with **ChemML's `Explain` tools**\n"
    '\n'
    'The deep-model explanation block is adapted from `references/Explain_visualizations.ipynb`, so it uses the same native ChemML visualization patterns:\n'
    '\n'
    '- **DeepSHAP** local waterfall plots and global summary plots\n'
    '- **LRP** local and global relevance heatmaps\n'
    '- **LIME** local relevance bar plots\n'
    '\n'
    'Because this tutorial can use either fingerprints or descriptor tables, the explanations refer to whichever molecular features were selected earlier in the workflow.\n'
))

